-- title:
--   Comparison morphism for the base-changed projective Weierstrass model
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ and $K$ be commutative rings, let $W_0$ be a Weierstrass cubic over $T$, and let $f : T \to K$ be a ring homomorphism, so that $W_0.\mathrm{map}\,f$ is the Weierstrass cubic over $K$ obtained by applying $f$ to the coefficients. Write $\mathrm{projModelGradingCR}$ for the grading of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)\,R$ modulo the ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic, given by the images of the homogeneous submodules under the quotient map, and $\mathrm{projModelStrCR}$ for the structure morphism $\mathrm{Proj}$ of this grading $\to \mathrm{Spec}\,R$ (the canonical map to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the degree-zero part, followed by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the algebra map from $R$). Let $\varphi$ be a graded ring homomorphism from the grading of $W_0$ to that of $W_0.\mathrm{map}\,f$ such that the irrelevant ideal of the target is contained in the image under $\varphi$ of the irrelevant ideal of the source (the hypothesis `hφ` allowing the formation of `Proj.map φ hφ`), and assume `IsCoefficientHom W₀ f φ`, i.e. $\varphi$ carries the class of a constant $C\,a$ to the class of $C\,(f a)$ for every $a \in T$ and the class of $X_i$ to the class of $X_i$ for each $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a morphism $\theta$ from the fibre product of $\mathrm{pullback.snd}\,(\mathrm{projModelStrCR}\,W_0)\,(\mathbb 1_{\mathrm{Spec}\,T})$ with $\mathrm{Spec}\,f$ to the fibre product of $\mathrm{projModelStrCR}\,(W_0.\mathrm{map}\,f)$ with $\mathbb 1_{\mathrm{Spec}\,K}$, such that $\theta$ followed by the first projection and then by `Proj.map φ hφ` equals the first projection followed by the first projection of the inner pullback, and $\theta$ followed by the second projection equals the second projection. Thus $\theta$ is a single comparison morphism over $\mathrm{Spec}\,K$ commuting with the map of $\mathrm{Proj}$'s, not a morphism between self-products.
--
--   This is a compatibility ("plumbing") statement identifying the base change along $\mathrm{Spec}\,f$ of the projective Weierstrass model over $T$ with the projective model of the reduced cubic over $K$, in the form of a comparison morphism between the two fibre products that sit over $\mathrm{Spec}\,K$. It is used in the extension statement for Drinfeld data, [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.RawDrinfeldPair.exists_map_eq_and_isLevel_of_isLevel_map`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.RawDrinfeldPair.exists_map_eq_and_isLevel_of_isLevel_map), where level structures on the model over $K$ must be compared with those over $T$.
